WEBVTT

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:15.870
reminds you of Krypton, doesn't it?

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:16.870
Who are you?

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:23.710
The answer to many of your unanswered question.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.710
I seriously think you have the wrong farmhouse.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:27.710
I would have expected a girl raised by such as stilic

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:29.710
race to be a better liar.

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:32.710
That's you're just as transparent as Calell.

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:39.580
How do you know, Callow?

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:45.569
I've been watching.

00:02:45.569 --> 00:02:46.569
That life is in my past.

00:02:46.569 --> 00:02:51.360
Only because you have no option to return, but you would, wouldn't you?

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:58.259
You have to miss the way things used to be.

00:02:58.259 --> 00:03:05.379
Memory back must have been a disappointment.

00:03:05.379 --> 00:03:08.699
I like my life here.

00:03:08.699 --> 00:03:12.300
And I think you should leave.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.300
That's a valiant effort.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:26.259
What if I told you that there was a way to go back,

00:03:26.259 --> 00:03:29.259
to save everyone you loved?

00:03:29.259 --> 00:03:35.250
I'd say you weren't the first Kryptonian to use those memories against me.

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:37.250
And it won't work.

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:45.020
That's unfortunate, because I need you.

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:49.360
That's not my problem.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:52.360
Well, at least you can't say I didn't ask nicely.

00:03:52.360 --> 00:04:12.840
If we'd have done this my way, no one would have gotten hurt.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:05:34.910
Why didn't you tell me there was another Kryptonian on Earth?

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:36.910
You're halfway across the country with no memory.

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:37.910
He's not a guy.

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:41.910
He's a machine. He's a... he's a... he's a computer.

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:45.180
Brainiac.

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:50.319
The last time I went up against this thing.

00:05:50.319 --> 00:05:53.319
He wanted me to release Zod.

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:56.819
But you destroyed Zod, right?

00:05:56.819 --> 00:06:02.759
What is he after now?

00:06:02.759 --> 00:06:04.759
Me?

00:06:04.759 --> 00:06:12.899
He made a lot of bad choices toward the end.

00:06:12.899 --> 00:06:15.899
Is it possible that he and Zod were allies?

00:06:15.899 --> 00:06:16.899
Never.

00:06:16.899 --> 00:06:17.899
If there's one thing that there's one thing that I'm not.

00:06:17.899 --> 00:06:19.899
If there's one thing that our fathers agreed on,

00:06:19.899 --> 00:06:21.899
it was their hatred for Zod.

00:06:21.899 --> 00:06:27.139
Why has he turned his attention toward you?

00:06:27.139 --> 00:06:30.829
I don't know.

00:06:30.829 --> 00:06:32.829
But when we go up against him,

00:06:32.829 --> 00:06:35.829
it would be helpful if we were all in the same playing field.

00:06:35.829 --> 00:06:40.329
Or should I say, Sky?

00:06:40.329 --> 00:07:01.660
Aren't articles supposed to have words?

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:05.660
Oh, I just start with the best part and work backwards.

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:07.660
Oh.

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:11.660
Well, my photo card has an equally big blank spot that's dying to be filled,

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:13.660
and I was just wondering if...

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:20.350
I'm wondering if, oh, if you need some eye candy to compliment those pros, but it looks like...

00:07:20.350 --> 00:07:21.350
Don't they put you guys on assignment?

00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:24.350
Yeah, yeah, the, um, the little stuff.

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:27.350
But now that the news is brought to you by Luther Corp,

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:32.350
I need something really, really big to stay off the gallows.

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:35.350
Don't worry, Lex couldn't hate you more than he hates me.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:39.350
So why not give him a double whammy?

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:45.040
Lois Lane and Jimmy Olson in their big debut.

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:49.060
What about Chloe?

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:54.060
Well, I know this will shock you, but Clark called and Chloe ran off on some big secret project.

00:07:54.060 --> 00:08:13.490
Okay, better make sure that camera is loaded with ammo because I got tomorrow's headline.

00:08:13.490 --> 00:08:16.490
Daughter of Nobel-winning astronomer murdered.

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:19.490
What, Swan Woman that they fished out of the lake last night?

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:21.490
Yeah.

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:23.490
I thought that she drowned.

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:25.490
More like Seg.

00:08:25.490 --> 00:08:27.490
Kind of hard to swim after you've been shot.

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:41.740
All the tracks are being covered, Mr. Luther.

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:44.740
No, we'll ever be able to trace the locket back to you.

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:45.740
I don't know.

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:46.740
need to remind you.

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:47.740
Absolute secrecy.

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:52.740
After this many years, trust me, I understand the magnitude of this moment.

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:56.250
It's funny.

00:08:56.250 --> 00:09:00.250
All those global treasure hunts and cave excavations.

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:04.250
And the secret of Veritas was so much closer than I thought.

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:07.250
I suppose it's poetic in a way.

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:12.250
Most things we spend our life searching for, usually are right in front of us.

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:18.419
There is one thing I don't quite understand.

00:09:18.419 --> 00:09:19.419
You say you've been searching your heart.

00:09:19.419 --> 00:09:21.419
You say you've been searching your whole life,

00:09:21.419 --> 00:09:24.419
but I thought you didn't learn about Veritas until recently.

00:09:24.419 --> 00:09:27.419
I've always known my father was covering a secret.

00:09:27.419 --> 00:09:32.419
A secret of cryptic symbols and mystic stones.

00:09:32.419 --> 00:09:35.419
I just didn't know it had a name.

00:09:35.419 --> 00:09:38.419
And what was it? The final piece?

00:09:38.419 --> 00:09:45.730
My own memory.

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:48.730
After the first meteor shower, there were years I blocked out.

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:53.730
But ever since I was shot in Detroit, I keep having flashes.

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:56.730
I keep having flashes of things that I'd forgotten.

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:58.730
And that's how you remembered that.

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:16.879
Your turn.

00:10:16.879 --> 00:10:18.879
But I just went.

00:10:18.879 --> 00:10:19.879
Howdy?

00:10:19.879 --> 00:10:22.879
Okay, okay, I'll go.

00:10:22.879 --> 00:10:26.879
10, 9, 8.

00:10:26.879 --> 00:10:53.500
Dr. Swan has been very open about the traveler.

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:54.500
Has he?

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:57.500
I feel like I'm trying to solve a puzzle with only a few pieces.

00:10:57.500 --> 00:10:58.500
He's keeping things from us.

00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:00.500
Lionel, he's being cautious.

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:03.500
And from the mutiny you're suggesting he should be.

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:06.500
Swan only tells us what we need to know.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:08.500
It's safer that way.

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:09.500
I understand.

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:13.500
But suppose it's all been a trick, a ruse.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:16.500
If we don't open that envelope,

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:21.500
Dr. Swan's conclusions could be as mythical as the gods at Mount Olympus.

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:22.500
Virgil's going to be here any minute.

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:24.500
I suggest you don't refer to his life's work,

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:26.500
is mythology.

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:28.500
Veritas.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:32.500
It's the greatest secret that world will ever know.

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:33.500
We formed this great secret.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:35.500
to use our wealth and power to protect that secret,

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:36.500
not expose it.

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:38.500
Is that Robert Queen talking or is that Virgil Swan?

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:40.500
You're sounding more like him every day.

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:42.500
Yes.

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:44.500
Dr. Swan made the discovery alone,

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:47.500
but that does not give him the right to keep it to himself.

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:49.500
Give me the envelope, please.

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:51.500
We promised that we would meet the traveler before

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:54.500
we decided to pursue a way to control him.

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:56.500
Don't talk to me about promises.

00:11:56.500 --> 00:11:58.500
You've been working in secret with Dr. Swan, haven't you?

00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:00.500
And you, Edward, you and Genevieve,

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:02.500
galliv galliv, galliv around the world.

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:03.500
You've been searching.

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:05.500
for those magical stones.

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:09.500
Lionel, this is bigger than the Queens or the Teagues or the Luthers.

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:14.500
Long before our family is united, men died protecting the secret of Veritas.

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:20.500
If Edward's ancestors are right, they've been sacrificing themselves to protect it for centuries.

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:25.500
If Dr. Swan's prediction is correct, the traveler is coming now.

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:27.500
We can't wait.

00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:33.970
That envelope and the secret inside it will give us ultimate power.

00:12:33.970 --> 00:12:34.970
You're afraid.

00:12:34.970 --> 00:12:37.970
You don't trust yourself with that, do you?

00:12:37.970 --> 00:12:38.970
Yes.

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:42.970
There isn't one among us who could resist that temptation.

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:44.970
We agreed.

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:48.970
We would not open that envelope unless the traveler proved to be a threat.

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:50.970
That's why Swan and I are flying to Zurich,

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:53.970
to make sure that the secret is kept locked safely away,

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:56.970
and ultimate power is left in the hands of the gods.

00:12:56.970 --> 00:12:57.970
Robert.

00:12:57.970 --> 00:13:41.980
Find the bank this key belongs to.

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:47.409
Sir, that could take months.

00:13:47.409 --> 00:13:49.409
Try 24 hours.

00:13:49.409 --> 00:13:50.409
It's a time.

00:13:50.409 --> 00:13:51.409
in Zurich.

00:13:51.409 --> 00:14:41.309
Comment on the death of Patricia Swan.

00:14:41.309 --> 00:14:42.309
Put the camera down.

00:14:42.309 --> 00:14:46.419
Put it down.

00:14:46.419 --> 00:14:47.419
Put it down.

00:14:47.419 --> 00:14:53.629
Very resourceful.

00:14:53.629 --> 00:15:00.629
I realize that an appointment or a press conference would be too conventional for you, Miss Lane.

00:15:00.629 --> 00:15:01.629
Oh, come on.

00:15:01.629 --> 00:15:04.629
You wouldn't take an interview with me if your life depended on it.

00:15:04.629 --> 00:15:07.629
So what makes you think I'll respond to an ambush?

00:15:07.629 --> 00:15:09.629
This is your chance to tell the truth.

00:15:09.629 --> 00:15:10.629
The truth?

00:15:10.629 --> 00:15:12.629
Before you're hauled away for murder.

00:15:12.629 --> 00:15:14.629
I can't decide.

00:15:14.629 --> 00:15:15.629
Is it boundless courage you have?

00:15:15.629 --> 00:15:16.629
Or is it?

00:15:16.629 --> 00:15:18.629
incorrigible stupidity.

00:15:18.629 --> 00:15:23.029
Potato-potto.

00:15:23.029 --> 00:15:25.029
You were the last person to speak with Swan

00:15:25.029 --> 00:15:28.029
before the poor woman ended up sucking pond water.

00:15:28.029 --> 00:15:35.039
This clever conversation is now over.

00:15:35.039 --> 00:15:39.039
Suit yourself, but I'm not going to be the only one asking questions.

00:15:39.039 --> 00:15:41.039
According to foreign records, you had five calls in one day

00:15:41.039 --> 00:15:44.039
from a woman who was previously sequestered overseas.

00:15:44.039 --> 00:15:46.039
It just happened to be the day that she ended up dead.

00:15:46.039 --> 00:15:49.039
Business calls, evidence of a business transaction, which it was.

00:15:49.039 --> 00:15:51.039
Oh, I don't doubt that.

00:15:51.039 --> 00:15:52.039
Look.

00:15:52.039 --> 00:15:56.039
Every photo ever taken of Patricia Swan shows her wearing his family locket.

00:15:56.039 --> 00:16:00.039
Now, not only was this locket missing when they fished her out of the lake,

00:16:00.039 --> 00:16:05.039
there was a burn right here on her neck where the chain was forcibly removed.

00:16:05.039 --> 00:16:25.009
Very sad. My heart goes out to her family.

00:16:25.009 --> 00:16:26.009
Mr. Luce.

00:16:26.009 --> 00:16:29.009
And now, if that is all from the dynamic duo,

00:16:29.009 --> 00:16:33.009
security, we'll be very happy to help you find your way out.

00:16:33.009 --> 00:17:29.529
Easy as bye.

00:17:29.529 --> 00:17:35.859
I know you sent Lana off to Isis if she wouldn't see your maiden voyage?

00:17:35.859 --> 00:17:51.119
When are you going to stop stalling?

00:17:51.119 --> 00:17:52.119
I'm sorry.

00:17:52.119 --> 00:17:53.119
No, I know.

00:17:53.119 --> 00:17:55.119
But it's just really easy.

00:17:55.119 --> 00:17:58.119
It's up, up and away.

00:17:58.119 --> 00:18:09.880
We don't have time for this.

00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:11.880
You saw Brainiac fly away.

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:13.880
How do you plan on catching him?

00:18:13.880 --> 00:18:15.880
It won't matter if we don't find him first.

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:18.880
Instead, we're wasting time with abilities that I don't have yet.

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:21.880
Fine. You cover the lands and I'll cover the sky.

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:22.880
I wish it were that easy.

00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:25.880
Chloe's been working overtime trying to help me locate Brainiac.

00:18:25.880 --> 00:18:27.880
And he just shows up with no one.

00:18:27.880 --> 00:18:28.880
morning.

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:37.160
He's got to be some way to track him.

00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:38.160
Power.

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:41.160
Everyone needs to be fueled by something.

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:46.500
He's not affected by the sun like we are.

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:47.500
So what does he run on?

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:55.230
Maybe energy.

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:56.230
He's a computer.

00:18:56.230 --> 00:19:35.150
Hello, Lona.

00:19:35.150 --> 00:20:36.579
Oh, let me go.

00:20:36.579 --> 00:20:37.579
Tell me they found her last night.

00:20:37.579 --> 00:20:45.180
I just walked through the door.

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:47.180
Another member of the Veritas clan silenced.

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:51.690
Chloe, do you think Lionel's behind this?

00:20:51.690 --> 00:20:52.690
I know he was throwing suspicion on the law.

00:20:52.690 --> 00:20:54.690
throwing suspicion on the Lex when you were captured,

00:20:54.690 --> 00:21:00.690
but nothing I dug up reveals any links between Lex and the Veritas clan other than his father.

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:02.690
Looks like all roads lead to Lionel.

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:04.690
What if she died?

00:21:04.690 --> 00:21:06.690
Protected me, Chloe?

00:21:06.690 --> 00:21:08.690
Protecting my secret.

00:21:08.690 --> 00:21:13.500
We don't have time for Gil right now.

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:21.640
Look, I spent the entire morning sweet talking the Centurion at the Department of Water and Power

00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:24.640
and he finally agreed to fast-track my password approval

00:21:24.640 --> 00:21:27.640
so that we could scan the power grids for any unusual surges.

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:31.640
Brazil, Honduras, Florida.

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:34.640
God, Braniac really gets around.

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:39.710
Oh my God.

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:43.049
What is it?

00:21:43.049 --> 00:21:47.049
A massive power surge flared up in Metropolis right near the ISIS Foundation.

00:21:47.049 --> 00:21:49.710
Lana.

00:21:49.710 --> 00:22:06.690
Clark, save it for the police.

00:22:06.690 --> 00:22:07.690
No, please.

00:22:07.690 --> 00:22:09.690
I came to see Lana.

00:22:09.690 --> 00:22:11.690
I'd hope that she could talk some sense into you,

00:22:11.690 --> 00:22:13.690
but we're running out of time, son.

00:22:13.690 --> 00:22:14.690
You must listen to me.

00:22:14.690 --> 00:22:16.690
You've already destroyed the life of one son.

00:22:16.690 --> 00:22:18.690
You don't get a second chance.

00:22:18.690 --> 00:22:19.690
The only real son you have.

00:22:19.690 --> 00:22:21.690
Hate you just as much as I do.

00:22:21.690 --> 00:22:24.690
That doesn't matter, but you've got to listen to me.

00:22:24.690 --> 00:22:25.690
Please.

00:22:25.690 --> 00:22:27.690
You're right, it doesn't, because you're just going to wash your hands of it.

00:22:27.690 --> 00:22:28.690
Aren't you?

00:22:28.690 --> 00:22:32.690
Just like you did when you murdered Dr. Swan and the Queens?

00:22:32.690 --> 00:22:34.690
You haven't changed.

00:22:34.690 --> 00:22:36.690
Patricia told me and you killed her for it.

00:22:36.690 --> 00:22:38.690
No. Clark, no.

00:22:38.690 --> 00:22:42.829
I never...

00:22:42.829 --> 00:22:47.829
But it's not important what you think of me, but I...

00:22:47.829 --> 00:22:50.829
There are some things that you should know.

00:22:50.829 --> 00:22:51.829
I have...

00:22:51.829 --> 00:22:54.829
You kept your secret hidden longer than you imagine.

00:22:54.829 --> 00:22:56.829
I should have listened to my father.

00:22:56.829 --> 00:22:59.829
I was stupid to think you could care about anyone other than yourself.

00:22:59.829 --> 00:23:02.829
You're less human than I am.

00:23:02.829 --> 00:23:06.829
Look, there's something I must give you. Here, take this.

00:23:06.829 --> 00:23:08.829
Please, nothing you have that I want.

00:23:08.829 --> 00:23:10.829
Now where's Lana?

00:23:10.829 --> 00:23:15.829
I don't know. The receptionist said she had a visitor and then she left.

00:23:15.829 --> 00:23:18.339
Visitor.

00:23:18.339 --> 00:23:36.279
Thank God you weren't at ISIS.

00:23:36.279 --> 00:23:37.279
I was afraid Brannick had gone there to find you.

00:23:37.279 --> 00:23:39.279
gone there to find you.

00:23:39.279 --> 00:23:40.279
Lana.

00:23:40.279 --> 00:24:20.420
So much for teamwork.

00:24:20.420 --> 00:24:22.420
Why'd you disappear on me?

00:24:22.420 --> 00:24:23.420
I thought you were going to check in with me

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:25.420
when you and Chloe found Brainiac.

00:24:25.420 --> 00:24:44.859
Look, what's wrong?

00:24:44.859 --> 00:24:45.859
It's a brainiac.

00:24:45.859 --> 00:24:49.460
He's done something.

00:24:49.460 --> 00:24:50.460
It was supposed to be me.

00:24:50.460 --> 00:25:06.410
Delivered Carol.

00:25:06.410 --> 00:25:08.410
Daily Planet.

00:25:08.410 --> 00:25:12.539
Monna.

00:25:12.539 --> 00:25:13.539
Lana.

00:25:13.539 --> 00:25:16.980
Lana.

00:25:16.980 --> 00:25:17.980
Monna.

00:25:17.980 --> 00:25:40.390
It takes the intrig of breaking and entering.

00:25:40.390 --> 00:25:45.019
So why do you think that Lionel's sharing

00:25:45.019 --> 00:25:48.019
his deep dark murder of secrets with Lana?

00:25:48.019 --> 00:25:49.519
He left his office and came straight here.

00:25:49.519 --> 00:26:01.339
Just look around.

00:26:01.339 --> 00:26:14.599
Lana?

00:26:14.599 --> 00:26:17.099
I'm sorry, but this is really...

00:26:17.099 --> 00:26:18.599
